<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Saxe-Römhild</h1><p class="st-meta">1680 CE – 1710 CE · capital Römhild</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived Ernestine duchy in southern Thuringia, one of the seven shares of Ernest the Pious's inheritance.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha">Ernest the Pious</a> of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> died in 1675, and his sons ruled jointly until they divided the lands in 1680. Henry, the fourth son, received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romhild">Römhild</a> near the Franconian border, establishing the small Duchy of Saxe-Römhild.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Henry rebuilt Glücksburg Castle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romhild">Römhild</a> and spent heavily on his court, leaving debts far greater than the tiny duchy's revenues. The territory was rural, Lutheran and administered by a handful of officials. Little else distinguishes its short history, which is known mainly from the disputes over its inheritance.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Henry died without children in 1710. His lands were divided among <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-saxe-gotha">Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg</a>, Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiningen">Meiningen</a> and Saxe-Coburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a> after a long dispute, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romhild">Römhild</a> later passed to Saxe-Meiningen.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-saxe-romhild.jpg" alt="Duchy of Saxe-Römhild" width="320" height="280"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_Duchy_of_Saxe-R%C3%B6mhild_(1680).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1680 CE – 1710 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Römhild</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sachsen-Römhild</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1695&amp;focus=duchy-of-saxe-romhild" aria-label="Duchy of Saxe-Römhild on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4921 427 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Saxe-Römhild lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5241 683L5244 667"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5244 667h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5241 683h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5241 683h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Römhild. <a href="/atlas?year=1695&amp;focus=duchy-of-saxe-romhild">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
